{"type":"message","id":"35c7f6bc","parentId":"ad2ab069","timestamp":"2026-10-17T22:51:10.107Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I fixed `parse_date` in `dates/parse.py`. The old `strptime` format had no field for the trailing `Z`, which is why it failed. It now uses `datetime.fromisoformat(s)`, and all 3 tests in `tests/test_parse.py` pass.\n\nWhat changes for callers:\n- **Timestamps ending in `Z`** now come back as UTC-aware datetimes. Timestamps without an offset still come back naive, as before.\n- **Mixing the two** can raise a `TypeError` if code compares or subtracts an aware value against a naive one. Nothing in this repo does that, but other code that uses `parse_date` could.\n- **Python version:** `fromisoformat` only accepts `Z` on Python 3.11 or later. The repo doesn't declare a required Python version; I tested on 3.13.5.\n- **Other inputs:** it's also more lenient than the old format. It accepts date-only strings, a space instead of `T`, fractional seconds and offsets like `+02:00`."}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"vertex-anthropic","model":"claude-opus-5-5","usage":{"input":2,"output":334,"cacheRead":26288,"cacheWrite":690,"totalTokens":27314,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0},"cttl":{"ephemeral5m":690}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1792277466148,"responseId":"msg_vrtx_011Cg8dP1SyAzbi6mTqbJqoa","duration":3958.164946000001,"ttft":3934.0233530000005,"contextSnapshot":{"promptTokens":26980,"nonMessageTokens":21589,"compactionEpoch":0}}}
